   "title": "How to use · v1.0.0",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How to use · v1.0.0\n\n**What it does:** makes a picture from a text prompt with MiniMax H3 Image, on the 12 GB files. Core ComfyUI nodes only.\n\n1. **Your inputs** (green group):\n   - **Prompt**: describe the whole picture like a photo caption: subject, place, light, lens, colours. Long, exact prompts work best. Text in quotes is drawn as text. There is no negative prompt.\n   - **Shape + megapixels**: the shape, and the size in megapixels (7.5 MP default, 3424x2304 at 3:2). MiniMax built the model for 4 to 20 MP (best near 16 MP); more MP = more detail and more time.\n   - **Seed**: fixed at 24112026. Type a new number for another picture; Run with nothing changed does nothing.\n2. **Models**: the three loaders must show the files from the Downloads note. Nothing to change.\n3. **Prompt**: nothing to change; the prompt and size come from group 1.\n4. **Sampling**: 6 steps, CFG 1, euler / simple. Nothing to change.\n5. Press **Run**. The **Result** node saves to `output/MiniMax-H3-Image/`.\n\n**What to expect:** 3424x2304 (7.5 MP) in 30 to 31 s; 16 MP (5024x3360) in 65 to 66 s. Times from the lab card, first run after start with the model load; files already in the system's file cache.\n\n**Tested on:** RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell 24 GB, 64 GB RAM, ComfyUI 0.45.3, inside a 10 GiB and a 12 GiB VRAM budget (--reserve-vram). Not run on an RTX 3060.\n"
   ]
  },
